<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim Iskandar of Johor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1958–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim Iskandar is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>, who succeeded his father in 2010, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-di-pertuan-agong">King of Malaysia</a>. Under Malaysia's system of rotating monarchy the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conference-of-rulers">Conference of Rulers</a> elected him the seventeenth Yang di-Pertuan Agong, and he took office on 31 January 2024 for a five-year term. A descendant of the temenggongs who became rulers of Johor in the nineteenth century, he is known for his outspoken defence of Johor's interests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-iskandar-of-johor.jpg" alt="Ibrahim Iskandar of Johor" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mikhail Tereshchenko · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Ibrahim_of_Malaysia_August_2025.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
